    "explanation": "This ruling refunds the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee to the rider.\n\nThe driver's arrival is confirmed and is not in issue. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02706) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius on 8 consecutive qualifying fixes from 12:51:17 to 12:52:24, closest approach 0.11 m, on a 100%-coverage, 10-second-cadence trace with no gaps, so POL-NS-02 is satisfied and the 'I'm Here' tap at 12:51:17 was a genuine marker, not a false one under POL-NS-05. No false-arrival referral is entered.\n\nThe fee fails on the waiting period. A no-show fee is chargeable only if the driver held position inside the geofence for a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period of 180 seconds (POL-NS-01(c), reading trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; the record carries platform_policy, so the defaults are not reached). Measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, as POL-NS-01(c) directs, the continuous dwell was 67 seconds (EV-GPS-02706, 8 fixes, 12:51:17-12:52:24) - 113 seconds short. The trip record's own timestamps agree: the platform started the wait timer at 12:51:19 and the driver terminated at 12:52:28, 69 seconds later. Limb (c) therefore fails, and limb (d) fails with it, because the trip was terminated before the required dwell had elapsed. The shortfall route of POL-NS-06 refunds the cancellation-fee line in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded.\n\nThe shortfall cannot be closed by accumulation under POL-NS-06(i): the trace shows a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1), and the only traffic advisory on file, EV-ADVIS-02706-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so no advisory exists that could permit separate intervals to be summed.\n\nOn the parties' claims. For the driver: arrival is established on admissible fixes, the marker is genuine, and no anti-farming issue arises (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 against 107 completed trips in 30 days, below both limbs of the POL-NS-07 check), so POL-NS-09(d) does not fire; those points are accepted. The driver's claim that limb (d) is carried is rejected - the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three limb (d) recognises, but limb (d) also requires termination at or after the dwell elapsed, which did not occur. The Driver Advocate's own concession that limb (c) fails with a 113-second shortfall is accepted. For the rider: the dwell arithmetic (180 seconds required, 67 seconds measured, 113 seconds short) is accepted, and so is the relief claim - EV-FARE-02706 shows the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 as charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), and the whole contested amount is returned. The rider's device track (39 qualifying fixes at 13.15-19.08 m from the pin, stationary through 12:48:41-12:54:24) sits inside the 100 m rider-presence radius and does not support the counterparty statement that the rider 'was not visible'; but rider presence does not decide this fee. Whether POL-NS-04 also exonerates the rider is moot: the rider's coordinating message at 12:52:17 and the driver's 'ok' at 12:52:32 make that clause's application arguable, but both POL-NS-04 and POL-NS-06 yield a full refund with no driver compensation, so nothing turns on it.\n\nNo profile field beyond the POL-NS-07 counters has been used to decide anything (POL-GEN-01); the mention of prior_no_show_flags in the driver's claim is a warning only, and that claim correctly treats the field as context-only. Evidence integrity is clean under POL-NS-08 (no clock skew over 90 seconds, no sampling gap, two chat messages matching chat_message_count, and the 4.50 fare line reconciles to the net figure), so no escalation arises and there is no contradiction between the trip record and the GPS trace under POL-NS-09(b). The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and is executed on issue."
